abstract: >
  A Python implementation of Vibrational Ramsey Theory,
  introducing frequency-based graph colorings that achieve
  polynomial bounds O(√(rs)·ln(rs)) compared to the
  exponential classical Ramsey numbers. Includes Z3-based
  verification tools for exact computation of R_ψ(r,s,ε)
  values and comprehensive test suites.
keywords:
  - ramsey theory
  - graph theory
  - combinatorics
  - z3 solver
  - sat solving
  - vibrational theory
  - frequency analysis
  - resonance
  - mathematical verification
